# PostPylot — Data Model

## Core Tables

`users`, `brands`, `platform_accounts`, `content_ideas`, `posts`, `videos`, `schedules`, `analytics`, `agent_logs`, `automation_rules`, `notifications`, `media_assets`

`workflows` from the product vision map to the existing `automation_rules` — do not add a
duplicate concept.

## Roadmap Tables (post-MVP, do not add yet)

- `templates` — reusable Remotion/Satori templates (add when the media phase needs them).
- `organizations`, `subscriptions` — multi-tenant + billing (Phase 13+).

## Enums

```prisma
enum Platform { youtube tiktok linkedin facebook }
enum ContentStatus { draft generated scheduled publishing published failed cancelled }
enum AccountStatus { connected expired disconnected error }
enum AspectRatio { horizontal_16_9 vertical_9_16 square_1_1 }
```

## Key Rules

- Every brand belongs to a user; posts/videos belong to brands.
- Platform accounts belong to users (not brands).
- Encrypt `access_token` and `refresh_token` before storage — never store raw tokens.
- Store platform metadata and agent I/O as JSON for debugging.
- AI generation requires at least one brand profile.
- Every table has `id`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, indexes, and foreign keys. Use soft
  delete where appropriate (brands, media assets) — never for auth `users`.

## Brand Profile Fields

name, industry, audience, tone, website_url, offer, content_goals, preferred_platforms, posting_frequency, forbidden_topics, preferred_cta, brand_colors, logo_url, video_style_preference

## Quality Gate (before auto-publish)

Score: brand relevance, clarity, platform fit, tone, duplicate risk, risk level, CTA, hashtags, media readiness.

**Block auto-publish if:** high risk, low brand relevance, empty content, media failure, expired token, duplicate recent content, missing required metadata.

## Content Status Flow

`draft` → `generated` → `scheduled` → `publishing` → `published` | `failed` | `cancelled`
